  "body": "Slice of #5670 (§8 of the Scaler-era data architecture revision, design PR #5667).\n\n**Row:** `~/tools/bin/atlas-search` wrapper (production entry: tries the laptop service on :18760, falls back to the nix-store Rust binary) → replaced by the fleet `search` domain entry once the serve role is stood up; wrapper retires.\n\n**State at filing:** the `fleet search` domain and the `fleet serve` search role both exist in the fleet binary. What is missing is the production-path proof: the serve role stood up on the laptop and the fleet entry serving production traffic.\n\n**Work:** stand up / verify the `fleet serve` search role on the laptop; verify `fleet search` answers the §8 Appendix A reference query comparably to the wrapper path; then retire the wrapper on the seat (and the laptop copy if one exists) and record the removal on #5670.\n\n**Acceptance:** serve role live on the laptop; `fleet search` verified against the wrapper on the reference query; wrapper removed; #5670 updated.\n\n<!-- pm-metadata:start -->\n```json\n{\n  \"direct_parent\": null,\n  \"links\": [],\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"design\": null,\n    \"roadmap_item\": null,\n    \"priority\": null\n  },\n  \"pm_meta\": 1,\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"queue_id\": null,\n    \"scheduled_start\": null,\n    \"picked_up_at\": null,\n    \"work_started_at\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-24T06:22:49Z\",\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"lane\": null,\n    \"host\": \"htch-runtime\",\n    \"worktree\": \"/home/hatch\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"lane_start_issues\": [],\n    \"workspace_ref\": {\n      \"kind\": \"worktree\",\n      \"id\": \"/home/hatch\",\n      \"repo\": \"developing-today/code\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"sha\": \"76bbec72135cee7bd837984b0cd283ae295766e0\"\n    },\n    \"auth_subject\": \"felix\",\n    \"stamped_by\": \"fleet 0.1.0 (native)\"\n  }\n}\n```\n<!-- pm-metadata:end -->\n",
